# DFZ offline install — settings for install.sh
#
#   cp config.env.example config.env
#   $EDITOR config.env
#   ./install.sh
#
# Every value here can also be given as an environment variable, which wins over
# this file — useful from CI or a config-management tool that should not write
# a credential to disk.
#
# Not mirroring into a registry at all? Skip this file and run
# `./install.sh --no-registry`.


# ── Your registry ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Where the images are pushed, and what the compose file will then pull by
# name. Host, optional port, optional namespace path — lowercase, no scheme and
# no trailing slash.
#
#   REGISTRY=registry.acme.local/dfz
#   REGISTRY=registry.internal:5000/dfz
#
# Use the SAME address your registry tells you to use for `docker login`. Some
# registries serve their Docker API on a port of their own rather than on 443;
# if yours names a port, it belongs here. Everything after the host is the
# namespace your images land in — install.sh checks the address before it
# spends minutes loading, so a wrong one fails in seconds.
#
# The namespace usually has to exist first: many registries reject a push into
# one they were not told to create. Create it in the registry's UI, and make
# sure the account below may write to it.
REGISTRY=

# Credentials used ONCE, for `docker push`. install.sh feeds the password to
# `docker login` on stdin, never as a command-line argument. Leave both empty if
# this host is already logged in, or if the registry accepts anonymous writes.
#
# Delete the password from this file after a successful install.
REGISTRY_USERNAME=
REGISTRY_PASSWORD=

# Where the library third-party images (redis, caddy, busybox) go. Defaults to
# docker.io/library. Postgres is a non-library image; mirror it separately via
# PGVECTOR_IMAGE (default docker.io/pgvector/pgvector:pg16).
# REGISTRY, which is what most sites want. Set it only if those are mirrored
# somewhere else — a shared pull-through cache, say.
#BASE_REGISTRY=
#PGVECTOR_IMAGE=


# ── This installation ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The URL people will open in the browser, and the one in-cluster agents dial
# back to. It must be reachable FROM YOUR CLUSTERS, not just from your laptop —
# `localhost` cannot work for a remote cluster. You can change it later in
# Settings -> Security -> Server URL without reinstalling.
#
#   APP_URL=https://dfz.acme.local
#APP_URL=

# Host port for the DFZ edge. This is the only port the stack publishes.
#UI_PORT=3080
